      "note": [
        "Methodological changes  \r\n- 2024-11-21: When publishing the reference quarter 3 2024, changes are implemented that aim to increase the quality of the statistics. The changes involve revisions, in most cases small, from April 2018 to August 2024 in several industries and aggregates. Part of this improvement is due to the enhancement of methods for constant price calculations from January 2022 and onwards, which affect the industries of Education (P), Human health and social work activities (Q), Arts, entertainment and recreation (R) and Other service activities (S) and all aggregates that include these activities.  \r\n- 2024-08-20: New decision-making rules have been introduced for the classification of head offices with extensive operations abroad or other Swedish corporate entities. The implementation will take place gradually, starting from the reference year 2022. As a result of the new decision-making rules, some large head offices have been reclassified as independent units and instead of support activities are regarded as primary activities. These kind-of-activity units are now included in the population with industry 70.1 head office activities. The change affects all aggregates in the statistics, which include industry 70.1.  \r\n- 2025-05-21: In connection with the publication of reference months January-March 2025, a change in methodology will be introduced regarding the handling of VAT data when used as a source of turnover. The change will entail revisions from April 2019 onwards, in most cases very small and not sufficient to affect published statistical values.",
        "The figures in the table have been revised due to a new model for seasonal adjustment and working day adjustment as well as a change in the reference year that was introduced 2013-02-28"
      ],
